      value: District emergency dispatcher
    - key: narrative.first_launch.speaker.radio.name
      value: DISTRICT DISPATCH
    - key: narrative.first_launch.speaker.radio.role
      value: EMERGENCY OPERATIONS
    - key: narrative.first_launch.speaker.samira.accessible_label
      value: SAMIRA HADDAD, CIVIL INFRASTRUCTURE
    - key: narrative.first_launch.speaker.samira.name
      value: SAMIRA HADDAD
    - key: narrative.first_launch.speaker.samira.role
      value: CIVIL INFRASTRUCTURE
    - key: narrative.gridlock.comms.01
      value: Fadi's service lane is usable. It was missing from my map. I have updated
        the route; local knowledge matters here.
    - key: narrative.m01.brief.aria
      value: 'Threat profiles: Courier carries orders, Warden controls the crossing,
        and Broker coordinates supplies.'
    - key: narrative.m01.brief.dalia
      value: 'First contact is confirmed: three armed Ash Line operatives are blocking
        the clinic corridor in Old Market.'
    - key: narrative.m01.brief.samira
      value: Civilians are sheltering beyond the patrol. Clear the marked corridor;
        do not pursue outside the district.
    - key: narrative.m01.comms.aria
      value: Courier, Warden, and Broker remain inside the marked corridor. Objective
        updates reflect verified mission state.
    - key: narrative.m01.comms.dalia
      value: Command squad, move to cover and confirm the armed patrol before engaging.
    - key: narrative.m01.comms.samira
      value: The evacuation path is holding. Keep the command squad intact.
    - key: narrative.m01.debrief.aria
      value: Recovered traffic includes a fragment of a revoked civic-relay credential.
        The source identity is unresolved.
    - key: narrative.m01.debrief.dalia
      value: The corridor is secure. The patrol was coordinated, not opportunistic.
    - key: narrative.m01.debrief.samira
      value: Civilians are moving to safety. Command Base is online; the next operation
        is ready for review.
    - key: narrative.m02.brief.aria
      value: Build a Barracks here, then train one rifle squad. That will make the
        post operational.
    - key: narrative.m02.brief.dalia
      value: This forward post is abandoned, but we need it. Restore it and prepare
        to defend the clinic road.
    - key: narrative.m02.brief.samira
      value: The clinic and city crews use this road. Holding the post keeps their
        route open.
    - key: narrative.m02.comms.aria
      value: We found a city access list on one attacker. It was copied before the
        first strike.
    - key: narrative.m02.comms.dalia
      value: Enemy patrol approaching from the west. Hold the post and keep them
        away from the clinic road.
    - key: narrative.m02.comms.samira
      value: It marks power stations, service gates, and tunnels. Someone stole it
        before the attack.
    - key: narrative.m02.debrief.aria
      value: The warning network ahead has gone dark. Armored vehicles are moving
        toward the next sector.
    - key: narrative.m02.debrief.dalia
      value: Commander, Dalia Rahim. I will lead the ground response from this post.
    - key: narrative.m02.debrief.samira
      value: The post is active again. The clinic road and city response teams are
        connected.
    - key: narrative.m03.brief.01
      value: The warning sector is offline. Scouts report an armored convoy on the
        western road. Our Ground Radar Tank can confirm vehicles once they enter
        coverage.
    - key: narrative.m03.brief.02
      value: Hold them at the junction or defend closer to the post. Keep the clinic
        corridor open. Even an unarmed carrier must not reach the inner core.
    - key: narrative.m03.brief.03
      value: We have roughly a minute to prepare. Two rifle squads and a working
        Barracks are ready. Choose a Tower, a Barrier, or reinforcements. The first
        warning is an estimate.
    - key: narrative.m03.comms.01
      value: The convoy's departure report matches the warning outage. The timing
        suggests advance knowledge. Keep defending; we will compare the records afterward.
    - key: narrative.m03.debrief.01
      value: The convoy is stopped and the post still stands. Check the damage and
        account for everyone. We need an accurate report.
    - key: narrative.m03.debrief.02
      value: The recovered orders name the warning outage before it happened. That
        is evidence of advance knowledge. It does not yet tell us who supplied it.
    - key: narrative.m03.debrief.03
      value: A medical and engineering team is cut off beyond the road. They need
        an airlift. Prepare a safe route for them.
    - key: narrative.m03.debrief.civilian.loss
      value: The convoy is stopped and the post is undamaged. We lost civilians.
        Record the losses and secure the clinic corridor.
    - key: narrative.m03.debrief.clean
      value: The convoy is stopped. The post is undamaged, and every civilian is
        accounted for. Keep the clinic corridor open.
    - key: narrative.m03.debrief.damaged
      value: The convoy is stopped and every civilian is safe. The post took damage.
        Repair it before the next response.
    - key: narrative.m03.debrief.mixed
      value: The convoy is stopped, but the post took damage and civilians were lost.
        Record both. The corridor still needs protection.
    - key: narrative.m04.brief.01
      value: Captain Laila Nasser. My helicopter is ready at the eastern landing
        area. Bring the four specialists to me in the APC; I can keep this extraction
        window open for ten minutes.
    - key: narrative.m04.brief.02
      value: Two medics and two engineers are stranded by the western road. They
        are the people who can reopen the clinics and restore the network. Bring
        every one of them home.
    - key: narrative.m04.brief.03
      value: Rifles cover the road; the APC carries the team. Unload beside Laila,
        board the helicopter, hold the area clear for twenty seconds, then fly to
        the marked departure zone.
    - key: narrative.m04.comms.01
      value: All four are aboard. The landing area is clear and departure is authorized.
        Fly to the marked exit; I will take the team from there.
    - key: narrative.m04.debrief.01
      value: Four passengers accounted for. Your escort gave us the time we needed.
        I am joining this operation; you will have an airlift pilot when the next
        team needs a way out.
    - key: narrative.m04.debrief.02
      value: The engineers brought their repair records. Several outages lead back
        to the same fortified communications node. We finally have a place to investigate.
    - key: narrative.m04.debrief.03
      value: 'Extraction confirmed. Captain Nasser is on the roster. Next objective:
        assess that communications node. First, let the medical team get back to
        work.'
    - key: narrative.m05.brief.01
      value: The engineers traced the outages to this fortified relay. Break the
        road gate, disable its transmitter, and secure the archive. Those records
        can tell us who ordered the attacks.
    - key: narrative.m05.brief.02
      value: Two rifle squads and a heavy APC are yours. Use the armor to open the
        gate, then bring the rifles through together. Preserve the APC if you can;
        losing it does not end the assault.
    - key: narrative.m05.brief.03
      value: The relay will erase its archive in twelve minutes. Stop the transmitter,
        defeat the responding guard, and hold the marked archive area for twenty
        clear seconds. I will guide each action.
    - key: narrative.m05.comms.01
      value: The archive is intact. I have recovered Protocol Fragment One. Its authorization
        record includes a credential issued to me, then revoked before these attacks.
    - key: narrative.m05.debrief.01
      value: The relay is silent and the records are safe. We have evidence now,
        not another rumor. Take care of the wounded; the city needs everyone we can
        bring home.
    - key: narrative.m05.debrief.02
      value: "The credential was revoked. Someone used its signature anyway. One
        encrypted message survived: \u201CQassem. The first node is lost.\u201D I
        cannot yet identify the sender."
    - key: narrative.m05.debrief.03
      value: First Response is complete. The reconnaissance team and armor parts
        are assigned to your roster. Review your results, then return to the campaign
        map. We will follow the evidence.
